# Keep the build context small. NOTICE, LICENSE, configs/ and docs/ are
# deliberately NOT excluded: the Dockerfile copies NOTICE and LICENSE into the
# image, which the AGPL requires to travel with the binary.
#
# web/ is not excluded either — the frontend stage builds it. These two are,
# and the first one is not an optimisation:

.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode

bin/
*.exe
*.test

# Local secrets must never enter a build context.
.env
configs/notifyrelay.yaml

# web/node_modules MUST be excluded, and a build that gets this wrong fails in a
# way that reads like a broken project rather than a broken context: the
# frontend stage runs `COPY web/ ./` after `npm ci`, so a host node_modules
# would overwrite the container's. esbuild and rollup ship native binaries, and
# a Windows checkout's would fail on linux/amd64 with an error about the wrong
# platform. It is also a couple of hundred megabytes of context.
web/node_modules/

# And the build output, because the Dockerfile builds it rather than taking
# whatever happens to be on the machine. A stale dist/ in the context would be
# embedded instead of the one just built, so the image would serve an interface
# from before the last source change — with nothing anywhere saying so.
web/dist/
